  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Voyxact (sibeprenlimab-szsi), an APRIL blocker, effective 2026-06-01. Approval criteria and explicit denials encoded; supporting clinical documentation requires manual review.",
    "Accelerated approval based on proteinuria reduction. It has not been established whether Voyxact slows kidney function decline over the long-term in IgAN. Continued approval may depend on verification and description of clinical benefit in a confirmatory clinical trial.",
    "Cautions (notes only): immunosuppression increases infection risk; monitor for signs and symptoms of infection. Live vaccines are not recommended within 30 days of treatment initiation or during therapy. Common adverse reactions include upper respiratory tract infection and injection site erythema.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 6 months; reauthorization up to 12 months. Manual review required.",
    "Quantity (notes only): one 400mg/2ml syringe every 28 days. Manual review required."
  ],
